.TH SCP-HEALTH 1 "October 2026" "sangfor-scp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scp-health \- read-only health report for a Sangfor Cloud Platform (SCP)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scp-health
[\fB\-\-days\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-cpu\-scan\fR]
[\fB\-\-workers\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-max\-rps\fR \fIRATE\fR]
[\fB\-\-top\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-csv\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB\-\-json\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-env\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-q\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scp-health
connects to the SCP Open-API and prints a text summary of the platform state:
open alarms, VM disk usage, failed tasks grouped by cause, host CPU
generations, memory pressure, capacity and lost VMs.
.PP
It only performs read (GET) requests and never changes anything on the
platform. Progress messages are written to standard error, the report to
standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-days " N"
Number of days of task history to examine (default: 30).
.TP
.B \-\-cpu\-scan
Also fetch the CPU type of every HCI virtual machine. This needs one request
per VM and can be slow on large platforms.
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Number of parallel requests used by \fB\-\-cpu\-scan\fR (default: 4).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-rps " RATE"
Maximum number of requests per second (default: 8; the API limit is 10).
.TP
.BI \-\-top " N"
Number of rows shown per report section (default: 15).
.TP
.BI \-\-csv " DIR"
Also write the report as CSV files into directory \fIDIR\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-json " FILE"
Also write the raw report as JSON to \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-env " FILE"
Read credentials from \fIFILE\fR (default: \fI.env\fR in the current
directory). Variables already set in the environment take precedence.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Do not print progress messages.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Credentials are read from the environment or from the \fB\-\-env\fR file,
one \fIKEY\fR=\fIVALUE\fR per line.
.TP
.B SCP_HOST
Base URL of the SCP platform, for example \fIhttps://192.0.2.10\fR. Required.
.TP
.BR SCP_ACCESS_KEY ", " SCP_SECRET_KEY
Access key and secret key for EC2 (AWS4-HMAC-SHA256) authentication.
.TP
.BR SCP_USERNAME ", " SCP_PASSWORD
User name and password for token authentication, used when no access key is
set. Requires the pycryptodomex (or pycryptodome) Python module.
.TP
.B SCP_REGION
Region used for EC2 signing (default: \fIcn-south-1\fR).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non-zero if credentials are missing or an API request fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
scp-health
scp-health \-\-days 7 \-\-csv report/
scp-health \-\-cpu\-scan \-\-workers 4 \-\-csv report/
.fi
.SH SECURITY
TLS certificates are not verified, because SCP platforms ship with a
self-signed certificate by default. Keep the \fB\-\-env\fR file readable only by
its owner.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/erelbi/sangfor-scp
